<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meroë</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meroe was an ancient city on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> from around the sixth century BCE. It was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-smelting">iron production</a> and trade, famous for its pyramids. Meroe declined in the fourth century CE, as the rising Aksumite kingdom extended its power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meroe.jpg" alt="Meroë" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wufei07 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NubianMeroePyramids30sep2005(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
